DEVICE              : NASKUR DETONATOR

AREA OF APPLICATION : STARS OF THE 
SPECTRAL CLASSES G0 TO G9.

MODE OF OPERATION   : PRODUCES A FIELD
WHICH PARTIALLY WEAKENS WEAK AND STRONG
ATOMIC POWER AND SO CAUSES A 
SPOMTANEOUS DETONATION OF THE TARGET
STAR. THE FIELD CAN ONLY BE SET UP FAR
FROM INTERFERING GRAVITATIONAL FIELDS,
AS OTHERWISE THE EFFECTIVENESS IS 
GREATLY DIMINISHED AND THE SHIP WILL BE
DESTROYED BY THE SUPERNOVA.

DURATION OF EFFECT  : AFTER A RADIATION
PERIOD OF 71 TORYN THE NOVA PROCESS IS
IRREVERSIBLY TRIGGERED OFF.

POWER SUPPLY     : MINI TARYNPENETRATOR

CONTROL          : CORUR-NASKUR, DECK 5

THE IGNITOR CAN ONLY BE DEACTIVATED BY
A COMPUTER WITH PRIORITY STATUS ALPHA 
THREE OR HIGHER. IN THE CASE OF A 
SYSTEMS BREAKDOWN OF THE MAIN COMPUTER
THE CORUR-NASKUR TAKES OVER DIRECTLY.
